# There is no admin panel, admin API, backend, or database anywhere in
# this project (grepped the whole repo — confirmed) — it's a pure static
# Vite/React build with no server-side code at all (see wrangler.jsonc's
# own "no main field... no server-side script" comment). /admin returning
# HTTP 200 was never an actual admin interface being exposed; it's this
# SPA's own catch-all fallback (wrangler.jsonc's
# not_found_handling: "single-page-application") rendering the exact
# same branded "Page Not Found" page it renders for ANY unmatched path
# (a typo'd URL, the old removed /reservations route, etc.) — necessary
# so real in-app routes like /menu survive a hard refresh, but it also
# means a scanner checking status codes alone can't tell "/admin" apart
# from "/anything-else-that-doesn't-exist".
#
# Cloudflare's _redirects format can't serve content with a custom (e.g.
# 404) status code — only true redirects (301/302/303/307/308) or a 200
# proxy — so the fix here is to redirect these specific paths straight to
# the homepage instead of letting them fall through to the SPA at all.
# That removes any ambiguity for both scanners and real recon attempts:
# nothing is ever served at these paths, full stop. Every other genuinely
# unmatched path (real 404s, typos) keeps its normal SPA "Page Not Found"
# experience — this list is intentionally narrow, not a blanket change to
# 404 handling.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
/admin         /   301
/admin/*       /   301
/wp-admin/*    /   301
/wp-login.php  /   301
/.env          /   301
/.git/*        /   301
/phpmyadmin/*  /   301
/config/*      /   301
